DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI LiveLogsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) driving a live SSE-style feed
through an injectable `LiveLogStreamSource` seam (default = a sample feed that filters by
level+grep and holds the socket open with heartbeats; production binds the shared KMP SSE core
per ADR-004/009). Four adaptive GlassPanels (filters / controls / conditional error / log table)
reproduce the web chrome; the table is a native columnar grid (macOS/iPad) ↔ per-row cards
(iPhone) with a pinned header, bounded scroll, tail-following autoscroll, severity-toned level
chips, key=value field chips with +N overflow, and regex grep-match highlighting. Rolling 1000-
event FIFO buffer, drops counter, pause/resume (connection kept), clear, and a .txt fileExporter
download all match the web hook. Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with
the web key names; full VoiceOver labels/traits; Dynamic Type via teslaSyncTheme; ADR-013
staleness chip. Reachable + deep-linkable via the new .liveLogs route (System group; alias
/admin/logs). Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift-6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0
macOS + iOS + DEBUG previews) and an executed model harness (36/36). The full xcodebuild scheme is
RED ONLY due to a pre-existing, out-of-scope swift-frontend IR crash (forbidden to commit-fix),
with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

